{"ts": "2026-06-05T08:01:22+00:00", "note": "CRITICAL: The `! E` sugar form (`returns i64 ! FileError`) currently does NOT wrap ret_ty into `Result of i64, FileError`. The function's `ret` stays `i64` and errors are tracked separately in `current_fn_declared_errors`/`error_types` (old effect model). Per spec \u00a73, `! E` must BE `Result of R, E`. This wrapping must be implemented here: in src/typer/lower/decl.rs (~line 332-419), when f.error_types is non-empty, wrap `ret` into the monomorphized `Result of R, E` enum before lowering the body, so callers see a Result, `?>` works on the sugar form, and match-exhaustiveness over Ok/Err is correct. Currently `match read(true)` on a `! E` fn fails with \"non-exhaustive match on I64\". The `?>` operator (2-3) and From conversion already work fully with the explicit `Result of T, E` form (tests/error_effects.rs, 12 passing)."}
